      "problem": "$$\n\n$\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡2\\sqrt{3}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡2\\sqrt{3} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{{(2\\sqrt{3})}^{2}-1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{12-1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{11}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
